From 28ff3a955b190c6c9cea8fcb393b7e02a775930d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LegendaryFire <tristan.balon@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 02:19:13 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Read Inkling 2's prompts with one-pass tensor-core attention

A prompt chunk's attention ran two passes (Q.K twice, for the maxima
and then the sums) over 16 queries x 3 heads a block, with the
relative bias's products on every key tile, so at 49K a full-attention
visit took ~330 ms of a 1024-token chunk (68% of its kernel time). Now
it is FlashAttention-2 shaped: a block is 128 rows (token x query
head) of one KV head, 8 warps of 16; Q is held in registers and K and
V come in 64-key tiles converted from int8 once a block (Q's shared
memory reused); S, an online softmax and P V run on mma.sync with P
kept in registers; the bias is only computed on tiles within its range.
The next tile (int8 rows and scales, or the sliding-window visits'
FP16 rows) is copied in (cp.async, two buffers) while the GPU works on
this one, the expert GEMM runs on mma.sync (warps of 32 x 32), and k_group places each
routed entry in parallel (it was a loop on one thread). The running
(O, m, l) between the tiered blocks and the resident ring is as
before.

With two cards, prompt chunks run on two executors at once
(--prefill-pipe, on by default): chunk c on executor c % 2, each on a
thread of its own, chunk c's visit v waiting for chunk c - 1's (its
cache cells and conv state), so while a chunk runs its layers on one
card the next runs on the other. A prompt's window grows only into
free VRAM: a chunk runs every expert, so one in RAM is copied in for
every chunk, while a cache cell in RAM costs it 264 bytes a visit; the
first decode step takes experts' room for the window as before. In the pool (--kv-resident auto) the auto prompt chunk
keeps a smaller margin, so 2048 fits beside two 512K sessions.

2x RTX 3060, UD-Q4_K_XL, 2 lanes at 512K context: a chunk at 49K
387 -> 954 tok/s (2048 tokens a chunk), 4096 tokens at 150K 585 ->
991, an 8K prompt 1260 -> 1567 (greedy tokens identical with and
without --prefill-pipe), 4096 tokens at the start 1150 -> 1712.
24K text, last 3.8K tokens after a 20K prompt: nll 1.415 (1.416
before; run to run about +-0.01).
